JXp-italic" id="MJXp-Span-15">i</span><span class="MJXp-mo" id="MJXp-Span-16" style="margin-left: 0.333em; margin-right: 0.333em;"><</span><span class="MJXp-mi MJXp-italic" id="MJXp-Span-17">n</span></span></span>$1 \le i  \lt  n$) such that <span class="MathJax_Preview" style="color: inherit;"><span class="MJXp-math" id="MJXp-Span-18"><span class="MJXp-msubsup" id="MJXp-Span-19"><span class="MJXp-mi MJXp-italic" id="MJXp-Span-20" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">s</span><span class="MJXp-mi MJXp-italic MJXp-script" id="MJXp-Span-21" style="vertical-align: -0.4em;">i</span></span><span class="MJXp-msubsup" id="MJXp-Span-22"><span class="MJXp-mi MJXp-italic" id="MJXp-Span-23" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">s</span><span class="MJXp-mrow MJXp-script" id="MJXp-Span-24" style="vertical-align: -0.4em;"><span class="MJXp-mi MJXp-italic" id="MJXp-Span-25">i</span><span class="MJXp-mo" id="MJXp-Span-26">+</span><span class="MJXp-mn" id="MJXp-Span-27">1</span></span></span><span class="MJXp-mo" id="MJXp-Span-28" style="margin-left: 0.333em; margin-right: 0.333em;">=</span><span class="MJXp-mrow" id="MJXp-Span-29"><span class="MJXp-mo MJXp-mono" id="MJXp-Span-30" style="margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0em;">(</span><span class="MJXp-mo MJXp-mono" id="MJXp-Span-31" style="margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0em;">)</span></span></span></span>$s_i s_{i+1} = \mathtt{()}$. </li><li> Let <span class="MathJax_Preview" style="color: inherit;"><span class="MJXp-math" id="MJXp-Span-32"><span class="MJXp-msup" id="MJXp-Span-33"><span class="MJXp-mi MJXp-italic" id="MJXp-Span-34" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">s</span><span class="MJXp-mo MJXp-script" id="MJXp-Span-35" style="vertical-align: 0.5em;">′</span></span></span></span>$s'$ denote the string obtained after removing these two characters from <span class="MathJax_Preview" style="color: inherit;"><span class="MJXp-math" id="MJXp-Span-36"><span class="MJXp-mi MJXp-italic" id="MJXp-Span-37">s</span></span></span>$s$. </li><li> Set <span class="MathJax_Preview" style="color: inherit;"><span class="MJXp-math" id="MJXp-Span-38"><span class="MJXp-mi MJXp-italic" id="MJXp-Span-39">s</span><span class="MJXp-mo" id="MJXp-Span-40" style="margin-left: 0.111em; margin-right: 0.167em;">:=</span><span class="MJXp-mrow" id="MJXp-Span-41"><span class="MJXp-mo MJXp-mono" id="MJXp-Span-42" style="margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0em;">(</span></span><span class="MJXp-mo" id="MJXp-Span-43" style="margin-left: 0.267em; margin-right: 0.267em;">+</span><span class="MJXp-msup" id="MJXp-Span-44"><span class="MJXp-mi MJXp-italic" id="MJXp-Span-45" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">s</span><span class="MJXp-mo MJXp-script" id="MJXp-Span-46" style="vertical-align: 0.5em;">′</span></span><span class="MJXp-mo" id="MJXp-Span-47" style="margin-left: 0.267em; margin-right: 0.267em;">+</span><span class="MJXp-mrow" id="MJXp-Span-48"><span class="MJXp-mo MJXp-mono" id="MJXp-Span-49" style="margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0em;">)</span></span></span></span>$s := \mathtt{(} + s' + \mathtt{)}$. </li></ul><p>You may perform this operation <span class="tex-font-style-bf">at most</span> <span class="MathJax_Preview" style="color: inherit;"><span class="MJXp-math" id="MJXp-Span-50"><span class="MJXp-mi MJXp-italic" id="MJXp-Span-51">k</span></span></span>$k$ times (possibly zero). It can be shown that <span class="MathJax_Preview" style="color: inherit;"><span class="MJXp-math" id="MJXp-Span-52"><span class="MJXp-mi MJXp-italic" id="MJXp-Span-53">s</span></span></span>$s$ remains an RBS after every such operation.</p><p>The <span class="tex-font-style-it">score</span> of an RBS is defined as the maximum number of consecutive opening brackets '<span class="MathJax_Preview" style="color: inherit;"><span class="MJXp-math" id="MJXp-Span-54"><span class="MJXp-mrow" id="MJXp-Span-55"><span class="MJXp-mtext MJXp-mono" id="MJXp-Span-56">(</span></span></span></span>$\texttt{(}$' in the string. For example, the score of the string "<span class="MathJax_